{title: The Good Wine Until Now}
{subtitle: John 2:1–11}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 120}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb6] [Ab] [G7] | [Cm7] [F7] [Bb] | [F7sus4] [Bb/F] | [Eb7] [F7sus4] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F7sus4]There's a [Bb6]wedding up in Cana on the [Dm7]third day of the week
The [Gm7]tables full of family and the [F7]music's at its peak
But [Eb7]the servants start to whisper and the [Dm7]steward starts to [G7]frown
The [C7]wine is running out before the [F]sun is going down [Bb6]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
His mother leans toward him, says [Dm7]they have no more wine
He [Gm7]tells her that his hour has not yet [F7]come, not yet the time
But [Eb7]she turns to the servants with a qui[Dm7]et knowing [G7]nod
Do [C7]whatever he tells you, and she [F]leaves the rest to God
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb6]You have kept the good wine [Dm7]until now
[Gm7]Six stone jars filled to the [F7]brim somehow
[Eb7]Water poured [Dm7]and wine [G7]came [C7]out
You have kept the good [F7]wine un[Bb]til [Bb6]now
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Fill the jars with water, [Dm7]so they fill them to the [Gm7]top
Now draw some out and take [F7]it, and they don't spill a [Eb7]drop
The steward takes a sip of [Dm7]it and calls the [G7]bridegroom near
Ev[C7]eryone serves the good wine first, but [F7]the best is only here
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb6]You have kept the good wine [Dm7]until now
[Gm7]Six stone jars filled to the [F7]brim somehow
[Eb7]Water poured and [Dm7]wine came [G7]out
[C7]You have kept the good wine [F7]until [Bb]now
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb7]The first of his signs at Cana in Galilee
[Bb]He revealed his glory for his friends to see
[C7]And his disciples be[F7]lieved in [Bb]him
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
You have kept the good [Gm7]wine
[F7]The good wine [Eb7]until [Dm7][G7]now
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
